/-!
# Examples

Concrete vertex (operator) algebras, in roughly increasing difficulty (Gannon §5.2.2).
"VOAs are notorious for having no easy examples" — these are the workhorses.

* `Heisenberg`     — the free-boson / Heisenberg VOA `𝒱(ĥ, k)`, central charge `1`
  (5.2.5).
* `Lattice`        — the lattice VOA `𝒱(L)` for an even positive-definite lattice `L`
  (5.2.2); odd `L` gives a vertex operator superalgebra.
* `Affine`         — the affine (WZW) VOA `𝒱(𝔤, k)` via the Sugawara construction
  (5.2.6); integrable for `k ∈ ℕ`.
* `VirasoroVOA`    — the Virasoro VOA and the minimal-model quotients.
* `MoonshineModule`— the Moonshine module `V♮`: central charge `24`,
  `Aut(V♮) = 𝕄` (the Monster), graded dimension `J(τ)` (§5.2.2, §7.2.1).
  Constructed in `VOA/Moonshine/` (`VOA.Moonshine.moonshine`); `Aut(V♮) ≃* 𝕄` is not proved.
-/
